WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Let’s measure an amount of time. We start at twelve and watch how many minutes pass.

2
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Fifteen minutes is a quarter of the trip around the clock. Fifteen minutes is one quarter of an hour.

3
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Thirty minutes is half the trip. Thirty minutes is one half of an hour.

4
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Forty-five minutes is three quarters of the trip. That duration is three quarters of an hour.

5
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:52.000
But quarter to four names a clock reading: three forty-five. It means fifteen minutes remain until four.

6
00:00:52.000 --> 00:01:02.000
An amount of time and a clock reading answer different questions: how long, and what time?
